The clinical and histopathological features are consistent with **targetoid hemangioma (hobnail hemangioma)**. The presence of **ectatic thin-walled vessels with papillary structures**, **swollen endothelial cells with intracytoplasmic eosinophilic hyaline globules**, and **positive PAS staining** for hyaline globules are characteristic findings of this entity. Additionally, **CD-31 positivity** and **collagen IV positivity** in the stroma further support this diagnosis. The absence of septa and irregular vessels on dermoscopy also aligns with this condition. Pyogenic granuloma and papillary hemangioma do not typically show the hyaline globules or the specific immunohistochemical profile seen here.

